.TH LOGIN 8
.SH NAME
login \- the console's login prompt
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /bin/login
(started by
.BR init (8))
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B login
only talks: it reads a name and a password (hidden) and asks the
accounts server,
.BR auth (8),
which checks the password and starts the user's shell as a child of
.BR login .
login waits for it to end; then the prompt comes back. It never sees a
hash. If login itself crashes, init adopts the running session and
starts a new login only once that session has ended: never two on the
console.
.PP
On the very first start there is no account at all. The accounts are
created on the screen, by the desktop's welcome screen; login says so
and waits. Only when there is no screen (no display card: the desktop
ended without one, or keeps failing) does login ask for root's password
and a first user itself.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/hostname
the name in the prompt.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR auth (8),
.BR sh (1),
.BR users (5)
